# CircuitPython Zephyr port — application Kconfig
#
# Sources Zephyr's main Kconfig. CircuitPython-specific symbol defaults live
# in modules/circuitpython-kconfig/Kconfig, a Kconfig-only Zephyr module: Zephyr
# merges a
# module's Kconfig right after the SoC/board defconfigs and BEFORE its kernel/,
# drivers/, lib/ and subsys/ Kconfigs, so the defaults there take precedence
# over any default Zephyr's subsystem Kconfigs define. This file is merged
# after all of Zephyr, where a Zephyr-side default would silently shadow the
# port's value (first `default` wins). Boards can override any of the defaults
# in their boards/<vendor>/<board>/board.conf file.

osource "$(ZEPHYR_BASE)/Kconfig.zephyr"
